! `si10-nc.in` again, with a prefix and a tighter threshold, as the starting
! point for `ph.x`: `si10-epsilon.ph.in` asks it for the dielectric constant,
! the Born effective charges and the **whole 30-mode dynamical matrix at
! Gamma** of a ten-site cell.
!
! It differs from `si10-nc.in` in three things and each is forced. A `prefix`,
! because `ph.x` finds the save directory by name. `conv_thr = 1e-12` rather
! than 1e-10, because a second derivative is worth converging further than an
! energy. And **`nosym`**, because `ph.x` refuses this cell with its symmetry
! on: `phq_setup` requires every operation to map the FFT grid onto itself, and
! the three-fold of a five-cell stack does not map a 15 x 15 x 80 grid onto
! itself (`warning: symmetry operation # 3 not compatible with FFT grid`,
! then `Error in routine phq_setup (1)`). With the symmetry off both codes run
! all sixteen points of the unshifted grid and symmetrise nothing, which is the
! configuration `defumat.response` accepts for a `nosym` run and the one that
! makes the comparison exact rather than a comparison of two wedges.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    prefix = 'si10'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 0, celldm(1) = 10.20, nat = 10, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 12.0
    nosym = .true.
    noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
 /
CELL_PARAMETERS alat
  -0.50  0.00  0.50
   0.00  0.50  0.50
  -2.50  2.50  0.00
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si    0.0000    0.0000    0.0000
 Si    0.2500    0.2500    0.2500
 Si   -0.5000    0.5000    0.0000
 Si   -0.2500    0.7500    0.2500
 Si   -1.0000    1.0000    0.0000
 Si   -0.7500    1.2500    0.2500
 Si   -1.5000    1.5000    0.0000
 Si   -1.2500    1.7500    0.2500
 Si   -2.0000    2.0000    0.0000
 Si   -1.7500    2.2500    0.2500
K_POINTS automatic
 4 4 1 0 0 0
